entry.summary:
Laravel has Stringable for strings, but numeric logic in apps often still looks messy. I just released laravel-numberable v1.0.0: a small package for fluent numeric operations and formatting in Laravel. Numbers in apps usually need more than + and -: parsing user input currency / percentage formatting rounding comparisons business rule helpers I wanted something chainable and expressive. composer require tresor-kasenda/laravel-numberable
$price = number(1999.99) ->withLocale('en_US') ->withCurrency('USD');
$price->asCurrency();
$total = number(120) ->add(30) ->multiply(1.2) ->round(2);
number(15)->clamp(0, 10); // 10 number(10.0)->trim(); // 10 number(17)->isPrime(); // true number(12)->isEven(); // true number(10)->between(5, 15); // true
number(0.157)->asPercentage(); number(1532000)->asAbbreviated(); number(1048576)->asFileSize(); number(21)->asOrdinal();
localized parsing (from('1 234,50', 'fr_FR')) when() / unless() pipelines macros and custom formats Laravel 10 / 11 / 12 PHP 8.3 / 8.4 Release: v1.0.0
Repo: github.com/Tresor-Kasenda/laravel-numberable
Feedback is welcome, especially around API naming and missing numeric helpers. Tags: laravel php opensource webdev
